@startuml
title realtime networking architecture (RN8 target)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
left to right direction

package "game / domain" {
  [Gameplay Simulation] as game_sim
  [Replicated View / Projection] as replicated_view
  [World / Relevancy Policy] as world_policy
}

package "Runenwerk integration" {
  [Application / Session Lifecycle] as app_lifecycle
  [ECS <-> RunenNet Adapter] as ecs_adapter
  [Preview Integration] as preview_integration
  [Presentation / Diagnostics] as presentation
}

package "external RunenNet" {
  [identity + protocol + session] as runennet_session
  [delivery] as runennet_delivery
  [replication] as runennet_replication
  [input / prediction contracts] as runennet_prediction
  [runen-net-quic] as runennet_quic
}

package "retained non-network Runenwerk concerns" {
  [engine_sim] as engine_sim
  [engine_history] as engine_history
}

game_sim --> replicated_view
replicated_view --> ecs_adapter
world_policy --> ecs_adapter
app_lifecycle --> ecs_adapter
ecs_adapter --> runennet_session
ecs_adapter --> runennet_delivery
ecs_adapter --> runennet_replication
ecs_adapter --> runennet_prediction
preview_integration --> runennet_delivery
preview_integration --> runennet_quic
runennet_quic --> runennet_session
runennet_quic --> runennet_delivery
presentation --> ecs_adapter

engine_sim --> game_sim : host simulation vocabulary
engine_history --> app_lifecycle : archive / replay integration

note right of runennet_replication
RunenNet is the sole reusable
realtime networking semantic authority.
end note

note right of ecs_adapter
Runenwerk owns concrete ECS/game/world
mapping and lifecycle composition,
not duplicate networking semantics.
end note

note bottom of engine_history
engine_net, engine_net_quic, and old
network authoring macros are absent
once their maintained consumers migrate.
end note

@enduml
